      "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"04c3b52c6cf76a06\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nOptic pathway gliomas are often quite vascular, and <strong>vascular endothelial growth factor (VEGF) promotes vessel formation</strong>. Targeted therapies such as bevacizumab, a VEGF inhibitor, have shown efficacy in controlling the growth of optic pathway gliomas due to their vascularity.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"04c3b52c6cf76a06\">>>",
